## Yalb Maeger v0.1.0

Minimal, frameless WebView2 browser for Windows.

### What's Included
- Single-file `.exe` — no .NET runtime install required
- Local startpage server (`localhost:3000`)
- Frameless window with custom chrome UI
- Tab management with session restore
- Vim-style keyboard shortcuts
- Debug logging

### System Requirements
- Windows 10/11 (x64)
- WebView2 Runtime (usually pre-installed on Windows 10/11)

### Keyboard Shortcuts
| Shortcut | Action |
|---|---|
| `Ctrl+Shift+Alt+F` | Zen mode (full frameless) |
| `Ctrl+Shift+B` | Toggle chrome panel |
| `Ctrl+Shift+S` | Toggle sidebar |
| `Ctrl+T` | New tab |
| `Ctrl+W` | Close tab |
| `Ctrl+L` | Focus address bar |

### Known Issues
- First launch may take a few seconds (WebView2 initialization)
- Icon may not show in Taskbar on first run (Windows cache)

